;; llvmi's eval level's classes (bin/llvmi check; doc/llvm/LLVM-CROP-SURVEY.md, "As built: llvmi (LL2's run, LL6, LL7)"), also AOT's
;; after test/llvm/divergences-aot.edn's: every row of test/llvm/check-{eval,aot}-linux-amd64.edn that does not pass, in goi's format
;; (GR10): a row is in the first class that names it in :tests or one of whose :match regexps finds its "RESULT REASON". :deferred, the
;; lowering's or ci's breadth still to build (LL5's list, survey §5.4, or C's crop); :design, by the survey's decisions. Read with the
;; Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :personality
  :title "modules that unwind: C++'s exceptions"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a module with a personality, invoke, landingpad or resume needs its personality's runtime (C++'s: libsupc++ lowered with the pending-flag layer, bin/cppi's runtime-build), which llvmi does not link on ci yet; the lowering takes these modules (bin/cppi lower-check runs them with gcc)"
  :decided "survey §5.3 (the personality as a parameter), LLS15 (a)"
  :match [#"^refused personality: "]}
 {:id :intrinsic
  :title "intrinsics outside the lowering's table"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the -O2 and C23 intrinsics the lowering's table lacks (llvm.fshl, llvm.scmp, llvm.lround, ...): the table grows by what the run corpora reach"
  :decided "survey §5.4, §6, LLS10 (a)"
  :match [#"^refused intrinsic: "]}
 {:id :va-arg
  :title "the va_arg instruction"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "clang lowers va_arg itself on x86-64; the instruction appears only in hand-written IR, and the lowering refuses it"
  :decided "survey §5.4"
  :match [#"^refused va: "]}
 {:id :datalayout
  :title "another target's data layout"
  :kind :design
  :why "llvmi runs x86-64 SysV's IR; a module written for another data layout (32-bit pointers) is read and printed, not run"
  :decided "survey §6 (class target), LOWER.md §7"
  :match [#"^refused datalayout: "]}
 {:id :target-type
  :title "target extension types"
  :kind :design
  :why "target(\"spirv.Event\") and its kind have no C type; another target's types are read and printed, not run"
  :decided "survey §6 (class target)"
  :match [#"^refused type: .*\(target "]}
 {:id :ci-builtins
  :title "ci's builtins: fmodf and the __atomic_* family"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the lowering writes frem as __builtin_fmodf and atomics as gcc's __atomic_* builtins (LOWER.md §7), which gcc takes and ci's builder does not have yet (arbace/c/build.ae's builtin-aliases lacks fmodf and fmodl; no __atomic_fetch_*): the program faults at the call"
  :decided "C's crop (doc/C23-SURVEY.md §6); this survey's Proposed"
  :match [#"undefined function (__builtin_fmod|__atomic_)"]}
 {:id :abi-punning
  :title "a lowered function called by native code through another type"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the lowering types i32 as unsigned (LOWER.md §7); musl's qsort calls the lowered comparator as int (*)(const void *, const void *): gcc's code reads the same register, ci converts the unsigned result to the pointer's int as a value, so -1 compares as 4294967295 and the sort differs"
  :decided "this survey's Proposed"
  :tests ["c-O0.synth.ext-callbacks" "c-O2.synth.ext-callbacks"]}
 {:id :ub-refinement
  :title "undefined behaviour refined otherwise"
  :kind :design
  :why "the program converts a NaN to an unsigned integer (C23 6.3.1.4p1: undefined; LangRef: fptoui of NaN is poison); the lowering refines poison as gcc's conversion, lli's JIT as its own (evidence: the program's own name and the conversions it prints)"
  :decided "survey §6, LLS9 (a)"
  :tests ["c-O0.run.nan-to-unsigned" "c-O2.run.nan-to-unsigned"]}
 {:id :argv0
  :title "argv[0]"
  :kind :design
  :why "the program prints its arguments: lli's argv[0] is the module's path, ci's the program's name"
  :decided "survey §5.2"
  :tests ["ee.MCJIT.2002-12-16-ArgTest"]}
 {:id :crash-report
  :title "both runs crash: the crash reports differ"
  :kind :design
  :why "the test expects arguments its RUN line passes (lli's run here passes none): both runs fault with the same status, and stderr holds each one's own crash report (lli's stack dump, cirun's or the AOT build's fault line)"
  :decided "survey §5.2"
  :match [#"^stderr .*(cirun|ciaot): fault: .* \| lli: PLEASE submit a bug report"]}
]
